--disable-librsvg is explicit, not incidental: obrender's configure.ac
treats librsvg-2.0 as an *optional* PKG_CHECK_MODULES (no librsvg means
SVG icon-theme support just doesn't compile in, not a build failure) - but
the previously-published openbox-3.6.1-1 package still ended up with a
real ELF NEEDED entry for librsvg-2.so.2 in libobrender.so, even though
this buildroot has never had a working librsvg package. The only way that
happens is the build sandbox's /host fallback PATH (used so builds can
reach host tools not yet packaged for ScrapLinux - see other recipes'
comments on this) let pkg-config see a librsvg-2.0.pc from the *host*,
outside the sandbox, and link against it - producing a binary that then
fails to load on a real ScrapLinux install, which has no such library. Force
the flag off so this can never happen again regardless of what the host
side effects to have installed. Revisit (drop the flag) once ScrapLinux has
its own real librsvg package - see ports/base/obconf-qt/recipe.local for
why that doesn't exist yet.
